Sent: Thursday, March 6, 2008 10:29:37 AM
Subject: [ballyalley] "Cold" Spray in a Can
















Mike White is sending me an Astrocade that overheats.  That is, it works for a couple of minutes and then quits.  He suggests that I turn on the Astrocade, let it warm up until the failing chip gets hot then feel around for the HOT chip.  This is all normal troubleshooting.  THEN Mike said to spray the HOT chip with a spray that comes in a can that cools off the "bad" chip instantly.  If the Astrocade comes right back on after spraying the chip then that is the bad chip.  Replace the chip and the Astrocade should be fine (unless, of course, what causes the chip to burn-out in the first place reoccurs).



Does anyone know what this cold spray in a can is called?



Adam

