5392:
The main problems associated with "intermittent" problems are:
1) loose connection to the power connector  inside the unit
2) Bad connection or wire to the RF modulator unit.
    a) There is a piece of copper under the  modulator  that may not be making  good contact 
    b) The 7 pin connector is not making good contact. try re-seating the modularor
    c) The long RF cable cable is not making good contact or has a break in it.
         Try rotating the connector where it enters the Modulator at least 1/4 turn
3) One or more of the custom chips has worked itself loose. Try pushing down on the 2 end of the chips firmly,
    but not super hard.
4) The cartridge connector inside is not "up to snuff". It may be dirty (Rubbing alcohol on a rag  usually cleans it fine)
    Or it may have 1 or more contacts not making contact well with the cartridge. This requires bending them up CAREFULLY. You'll need to take the unit most of the way apart, including the top and the large black plastic assembly that holds the keypad contacts. Be careful here not to loose the spring and not to break any wires going to the keypad.

If the above 4 don't seem to have any effect, the problem is probably a break in one or more circuits on the PCB. Those are HARD to find specially when it works most of the time.
I hope this solves your problem
Ken
