Lance,
(see, I got the name right this time)

Some of your "unclean" video may be due to the Arcade itself. 

When you put the program into a loop, the program run through the frequencies that are close to the screen video, and since the unit usually shares the screen ram with the stack and program space, you get a "wavy" background. 

Extended BASICS have their own stack and memory space, but DO share the same processor as the video. 
Some loops do come through wavy while others you won't see at all.

For video "screen shots" talk to Mike White about his Snoop Camera program. 
There may be a way to get what you want.
Ken

