Ken;

Lance was right, 300 baud WAS supported in the Viper, in fact as I
understood it, it was the 2000 baud routines that were the "last
minute" add. 300 baud uses :INPUT  :LIST  :PRINT  :RETURN  and *PRINT
same as old Bally Basic 6002. However, LILL' WHITE RAM won't be able
to access them as the 300 baud interface uses the lite pen jack for
power, and so does LILL' WHITE RAM. {note: DON'T try to "parallel"
the power hook up as the Arcades 5V supply isn't built to handle both
units at the same time}! As to the "PLAY" command, I've never tried
it, so it may be there. [more on this later] Also, there is a third
start in BRB mentioned (by me) before, and there is the hook to
another address from the screen interrupt service routine when the
note timer is set for it. (also mentioned by me before) I do not
believe Vipersoft has either of these features.

