Sent: Thursday, March 13, 2008 1:12:40 PM
Subject: [ballyalley] Re: Incredible Wizard prototype dump [was: Fondly Remembered BASIC Games from OTHER Pla

                  Well, the first byte is a $44 Hex, neither a $55 Menustart sentinel
nor a $C3 JumP instruction usually used in an Autostart cartridge.
Most of the bytes don't match the real Wizard binary, except for a
clump of "="s near the end and the letters "WIZ" at $3FF4 which is
all that's left of the text string "THE WIZARD". It's a bad dump. 

